{
  "id": "longest-common-subsequence",
  "questionId": "longest-common-subsequence",
  "slug": "longest-common-subsequence",
  "title": "Longest Common Subsequence",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Dp 2d",
  "patterns": [
    "dynamic programming",
    "strings"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "blind-75"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "think about comparing text1 and text2 character by character from the end (or start) - what happens when the current characters match versus when they don't?",
    "define dp[i][j] as the length of the longest common subsequence between the first i characters of text1 and the first j characters of text2",
    "if text1[i-1] == text2[j-1], that matching character extends the best subsequence found without it: dp[i][j] = 1 + dp[i-1][j-1]",
    "if they don't match, the character can't be part of a common subsequence ending exactly there, so take the best of dropping one character from either string: dp[i][j] = max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1])",
    "dp[0][j] and dp[i][0] are all 0, since an empty string has no common subsequence with anything; fill the table and return dp[m][n]"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "mixing up string indices (i-1, j-1) versus dp table indices (i, j), causing off-by-one bugs",
    "taking the sum instead of the max when characters don't match",
    "forgetting that a subsequence doesn't require contiguous characters, and accidentally solving for longest common substring instead"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given two strings. A subsequence is formed by deleting some\n(possibly zero) characters from a string without changing the order of\nthe remaining characters, and a common subsequence is one that appears\nas a subsequence in both strings.\n\n**Find the length of the longest common subsequence of the two\nstrings.**\n\nIf the two strings share no characters in common, return 0.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= text1.length <= 1000",
      "1 <= text2.length <= 1000",
      "text1 and text2 consist of only lowercase English characters"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "the two strings share no characters at all",
      "one string is a subsequence of the other",
      "the two strings are identical",
      "one of the strings has length 1"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
